@startuml
title The Three Identities - Who Is Acting, When?
skinparam componentStyle rectangle
skinparam defaultTextAlignment center

actor "**1. Developer**\n(your personal login)" as dev #E6F4EA
rectangle "**2. Deployment SP**\n(one per environment:\nstaging SP, prod SP)" as dsp #FEF7E0
rectangle "**3. App SP**\n(auto-created PER APP,\nper environment)" as asp #FCE8E6

rectangle "dev target" as t_dev
rectangle "staging / prod targets" as t_sp
rectangle "Running Databricks App" as app
database "Environment catalog\n(tables, volumes, warehouse)" as cat

dev --> t_dev : deploys & runs\n(inner loop only)
dsp --> t_sp : deploys bundles\n(SOP today, pipeline later)
t_sp --> app : app is created by deploy...
asp --> app : ...but RUNS as its own SP
app --> cat : queries succeed only if\nthe APP SP has grants

note bottom of asp
  #1 newcomer trap: granting catalog access
  to yourself or the deployment SP does
  NOT grant it to the app. The app's own SP
  needs grants in EVERY environment -
  "works in dev, 403 in staging" = this.
end note
@enduml
